A timeline places events on a chronological axis. Use it for version history, project milestones, and historical context. ''New in Mermaid 9.4.''

---

!! Basic example

```
timeline
    title Plugin Version History
    2021 : v0.3.2 — Mermaid 8.x
    2022 : v0.3.7 — Mermaid 9.3
    2024 : v0.3.8 — TiddlyWiki 5.3.3
    2026 : v0.4.0 — Mermaid 11.14.0
```

$$$text/vnd.tiddlywiki.mermaid
timeline
    title Plugin Version History
    2021 : v0.3.2 — Mermaid 8.x
    2022 : v0.3.7 — Mermaid 9.3
    2024 : v0.3.8 — TiddlyWiki 5.3.3
    2026 : v0.4.0 — Mermaid 11.14.0
$$$

---

!! Real-world example: Mermaid diagram types over time

This timeline groups Mermaid diagram types by the era in which they were introduced, using sections to assign a distinct background color to each period.

```
timeline
    %% ── Founding era ───────────────────────────
    section 2014 to 2020
        2014 : Flowchart
             : Sequence Diagram
        2018 : Class Diagram
             : State Diagram
        2019 : ER Diagram
             : Gantt
        2020 : Git Graph

    %% ── Growth era ─────────────────────────────
    section 2021 to 2022
        2021 : Pie Chart
             : User Journey
             : C4 Diagram
        2022 : Mindmap
             : Timeline

    %% ── Modern era ─────────────────────────────
    section 2023 to 2024
        2023 : Sankey
             : Quadrant
             : XY Chart
        2024 : Architecture
             : Kanban
             : Block Diagram
             : Packet
```

$$$text/vnd.tiddlywiki.mermaid
timeline
    %% ── Founding era ───────────────────────────
    section 2014 to 2020
        2014 : Flowchart
             : Sequence Diagram
        2018 : Class Diagram
             : State Diagram
        2019 : ER Diagram
             : Gantt
        2020 : Git Graph

    %% ── Growth era ─────────────────────────────
    section 2021 to 2022
        2021 : Pie Chart
             : User Journey
             : C4 Diagram
        2022 : Mindmap
             : Timeline

    %% ── Modern era ─────────────────────────────
    section 2023 to 2024
        2023 : Sankey
             : Quadrant
             : XY Chart
        2024 : Architecture
             : Kanban
             : Block Diagram
             : Packet
$$$

|!Section|!Meaning|
|2014 to 2020|Founding era — core diagram types|
|2021 to 2022|Growth era — new visual formats|
|2023 to 2024|Modern era — advanced and beta types|

''Note:'' each section's background color cycles automatically through the active theme palette — colors are not set in the source and change with the selected theme.

---

!! Syntax

```
timeline
    title My Timeline
    2020 : Event A
         : Event B (same period, second entry)
    section Next Phase
        2021 : Event C
```

* ''Period labels'' are free text — use years, quarters, sprint names, version numbers.
* ''Multiple events'' per period: indent additional `: event` lines under the same period.
* ''Sections'' group periods with a visual header. They are optional.

!! Tips

* Long event text wraps automatically.
* The `–` dash in period ranges is a display choice — the label is just text, not parsed.
* Sections help readability for timelines spanning many years.
* Avoid colons inside event labels — they are structural delimiters and will break parsing.

